From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cocoman93 <353537723+cocoman93@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:48:14 +0000
Subject: upstream-pr-2091: a one-off frame after a loading screen no longer
 steps the frame step up

nxnative PR #2091 (cocoman93, open): a frame whose cost is above every hold and that follows
a run of 30 frames on time starts a grace with no trial, so Ocarina of Time keeps the 60 fps
hold as Kokiri Forest appears after loading a save instead of dropping to 30 fps for about
a second.

NXForge on top: it sits beside NXForge's stall grace (fstep-stall); a stall or a frame the
caller names as settling keeps its own grace and is not counted as a one-off frame too. The
summary line counts both. t_fstep: 150 checks pass (Linux clang), including the PR's own and
a split of the "three 83 ms frames" check into after a run on time (a one-off frame now) and
after a late frame (steps up as before).

Co-authored-by: cocoman93 <cocoman93@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
